----- B (5.2s) -----
[verse]
The ferry drops us on the dock at Marianne Bay
The sun hits hard and washes the sweat from my face
I see the old red fort standing guard on the hill
And the tourists rushing toward the duty-free shop
They don't know the history of this concrete wall
They just want a drink before the sun goes down

[chorus]
I love this island, but it breaks my heart sometimes
I love this island, it’s hard to leave behind

[verse]
I drive past the Union Church where we got baptized
The paint is peeling off the wooden sides
I remember when my daddy fixed the fishing net
He said, "Boy, patience keeps you from going wet"
Now the nets sit empty on the dusty shore
Because the fish moved deeper than we used to go

[chorus]
I love this island, but it breaks my heart sometimes
